{
  "title": "ShipJS: Zero to Deploy",
  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "title": "JS Fundamentals",
      "description": "Variables, functions, arrays. Ship your first function.",
      "lessons": [
        {"id":"m1l1","title":"Console.log","type":"lesson","fileName":"hello.js","xp":20,"docs":"<p>Log <code>\"I ship\"</code></p>","starterCode":"// Log \"I ship\"\n","solution":"console.log(\"I ship\");","hints":["Use console.log()","Put string in quotes"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs 'I ship'","type":"log","check":"I ship"}]},
        {"id":"m1l2","title":"Variables: const vs let","type":"lesson","fileName":"vars.js","xp":30,"docs":"<p>Create <code>const shipName = \"ShipJS\"</code> and log it.</p>","starterCode":"// Create shipName\n","solution":"const shipName = \"ShipJS\";\nconsole.log(shipName);","hints":["const shipName = \"ShipJS\";"],"tests":[{"name":"Declares shipName","type":"regex","check":"const\\s+shipName\\s*=\\s*[\"']ShipJS[\"']"},{"name":"Logs ShipJS","type":"log","check":"ShipJS"}]},
        {"id":"m1l3","title":"Numbers & Math","type":"lesson","fileName":"math.js","xp":30,"docs":"<p>Log <code>10 + 5 * 2</code></p>","starterCode":"// Log 10 + 5 * 2\n","solution":"console.log(10 + 5 * 2);","hints":["Answer is 20"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs 20","type":"log","check":"20"}]},
        {"id":"m1l4","title":"Strings & Template Literals","type":"lesson","fileName":"strings.js","xp":30,"docs":"<p>Log <code>`Hello ${name}`</code> with <code>name = \"Coder\"</code></p>","starterCode":"// Template literal\n","solution":"const name = \"Coder\";\nconsole.log(`Hello ${name}`);","hints":["Use backticks"],"tests":[{"name":"Uses template literal","type":"regex","check":"`.*\\$\\{.*\\}.*`"},{"name":"Logs 'Hello Coder'","type":"log","check":"Hello Coder"}]},
        {"id":"m1l5","title":"Booleans & Comparisons","type":"lesson","fileName":"bool.js","xp":30,"docs":"<p>Log result of <code>5 === 5</code></p>","starterCode":"// Log 5 === 5\n","solution":"console.log(5 === 5);","hints":["Should log true"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs true","type":"log","check":"true"}]},
        {"id":"m1l6","title":"Functions","type":"lesson","fileName":"func.js","xp":40,"docs":"<p>Create <code>double</code> that returns <code>n * 2</code>. Log <code>double(5)</code></p>","starterCode":"// Create double function\n","solution":"const double = (n) => n * 2;\nconsole.log(double(5));","hints":["const double = (n) => n * 2;"],"tests":[{"name":"Defines double","type":"regex","check":"const\\s+double\\s*=.*=>"},{"name":"Logs 10","type":"log","check":"10"}]},
        {"id":"m1l7","title":"Ship Function Project","type":"project","fileName":"ship.js","xp":50,"docs":"<p>Create <code>ship(name)</code> returning <code>`Shipping ${name}`</code>. Log <code>ship(\"Code\")</code></p>","starterCode":"// Create ship function\n","solution":"const ship = (name) => `Shipping ${name}`;\nconsole.log(ship(\"Code\"));","hints":["Use template literal"],"tests":[{"name":"Defines ship","type":"regex","check":"const\\s+ship\\s*=.*=>"},{"name":"Logs 'Shipping Code'","type":"log","check":"Shipping Code"}]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m2",
      "title": "Control Flow",
      "description": "If/else, loops, ternary. Make decisions in code.",
      "lessons": [
        {"id":"m2l1","title":"If Statements","type":"lesson","fileName":"if.js","xp":40,"docs":"<p>If <code>5 > 3</code> log <code>\"Big\"</code></p>","starterCode":"// if statement\n","solution":"if (5 > 3) {\n console.log(\"Big\");\n}","hints":["if (5 > 3) {...}"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs 'Big'","type":"log","check":"Big"}]},
        {"id":"m2l2","title":"If/Else","type":"lesson","fileName":"else.js","xp":40,"docs":"<p>If <code>2 > 5</code> log <code>\"Yes\"</code> else log <code>\"No\"</code></p>","starterCode":"// if else\n","solution":"if (2 > 5) {\n console.log(\"Yes\");\n} else {\n console.log(\"No\");\n}","hints":["2 > 5 is false"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs 'No'","type":"log","check":"No"}]},
        {"id":"m2l3","title":"Ternary Operator","type":"lesson","fileName":"ternary.js","xp":40,"docs":"<p>Log <code>10 > 5? \"Yes\" : \"No\"</code></p>","starterCode":"// ternary\n","solution":"console.log(10 > 5? \"Yes\" : \"No\");","hints":["condition? yes : no"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs 'Yes'","type":"log","check":"Yes"}]},
        {"id":"m2l4","title":"For Loops","type":"lesson","fileName":"for.js","xp":40,"docs":"<p>Log 0,1,2 with for loop</p>","starterCode":"// for loop\n","solution":"for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n console.log(i);\n}","hints":["i < 3"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs 0","type":"log","check":"0"},{"name":"Logs 1","type":"log","check":"1"},{"name":"Logs 2","type":"log","check":"2"}]},
        {"id":"m2l5","title":"While Loops","type":"lesson","fileName":"while.js","xp":40,"docs":"<p>Log 0,1,2 with while. Start <code>let i = 0</code></p>","starterCode":"let i = 0;\n// while loop\n","solution":"let i = 0;\nwhile (i < 3) {\n console.log(i);\n i++;\n}","hints":["Don't forget i++"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs 2","type":"log","check":"2"}]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m3",
      "title": "Arrays & Objects",
      "description": "Store collections. Map, filter, reduce.",
      "lessons": [
        {"id":"m3l1","title":"Arrays","type":"lesson","fileName":"arrays.js","xp":40,"docs":"<p>Create <code>nums = [1,2,3]</code> and log <code>nums[1]</code></p>","starterCode":"// Create array\n","solution":"const nums = [1,2,3];\nconsole.log(nums[1]);","hints":["Arrays 0-indexed"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs 2","type":"log","check":"2"}]},
        {"id":"m3l2","title":"Array.push & length","type":"lesson","fileName":"push.js","xp":40,"docs":"<p>Create empty <code>arr</code>, push <code>\"ship\"</code>, log <code>arr.length</code></p>","starterCode":"// Push to array\n","solution":"const arr = [];\narr.push(\"ship\");\nconsole.log(arr.length);","hints":["arr.push(\"ship\")"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs 1","type":"log","check":"1"}]},
        {"id":"m3l3","title":"Array.map","type":"lesson","fileName":"map.js","xp":50,"docs":"<p>Double each number in <code>[1,2,3]</code> with map</p>","starterCode":"const nums = [1,2,3];\n// Map to double\n","solution":"const nums = [1,2,3];\nconst doubled = nums.map(n => n * 2);\nconsole.log(doubled);","hints":["nums.map(n => n * 2)"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs [2,4,6]","type":"log","check":"[2,4,6]"}]},
        {"id":"m3l4","title":"Array.filter","type":"lesson","fileName":"filter.js","xp":50,"docs":"<p>Filter <code>[1,2,3,4]</code> for evens only</p>","starterCode":"const nums = [1,2,3,4];\n// Filter evens\n","solution":"const nums = [1,2,3,4];\nconst evens = nums.filter(n => n % 2 === 0);\nconsole.log(evens);","hints":["n % 2 === 0"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs [2,4]","type":"log","check":"[2,4]"}]},
        {"id":"m3l5","title":"Objects","type":"lesson","fileName":"objects.js","xp":40,"docs":"<p>Create <code>user = {name: \"Ship\"}</code> and log <code>user.name</code></p>","starterCode":"// Create object\n","solution":"const user = {name: \"Ship\"};\nconsole.log(user.name);","hints":["Dot notation"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs 'Ship'","type":"log","check":"Ship"}]},
        {"id":"m3l6","title":"Destructuring","type":"lesson","fileName":"destruct.js","xp":50,"docs":"<p>Destructure <code>name</code> from <code>{name: \"JS\", year: 1995}</code></p>","starterCode":"const lang = {name: \"JS\", year: 1995};\n// Destructure\n","solution":"const lang = {name: \"JS\", year: 1995};\nconst {name} = lang;\nconsole.log(name);","hints":["const {name} = lang;"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs 'JS'","type":"log","check":"JS"}]},
        {"id":"m3l7","title":"Array Methods Project","type":"project","fileName":"methods.js","xp":60,"docs":"<p>From <code>[1,2,3,4,5]</code>, keep evens then double them</p>","starterCode":"const nums = [1,2,3,4,5];\n// Chain filter map\n","solution":"const nums = [1,2,3,4,5];\nconst result = nums.filter(n => n % 2 === 0).map(n => n * 2);\nconsole.log(result);","hints":[".filter().map()"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs [4,8]","type":"log","check":"[4,8]"}]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m4",
      "title": "DOM & Events",
      "description": "Make pages interactive. Query, listen, update.",
      "lessons": [
        {"id":"m4l1","title":"querySelector","type":"lesson","fileName":"query.js","xp":40,"docs":"<p>Create <code>getTitle</code> that returns <code>document.querySelector('h1').textContent</code></p>","starterCode":"// getTitle function\n","solution":"const getTitle = () => document.querySelector('h1').textContent;","hints":["Return querySelector"],"tests":[{"name":"Defines getTitle","type":"regex","check":"const\\s+getTitle\\s*=.*=>"},{"name":"Uses querySelector","type":"regex","check":"querySelector\\(['\"]h1['\"]\\)"}]},
        {"id":"m4l2","title":"addEventListener","type":"lesson","fileName":"events.js","xp":50,"docs":"<p>Add click listener to <code>button</code> that logs <code>\"clicked\"</code></p>","starterCode":"const button = document.querySelector('button');\n// onClick function\n","solution":"const button = document.querySelector('button');\nconst onClick = () => {\n button.addEventListener('click', () => console.log('clicked'));\n};","hints":["addEventListener('click', fn)"],"tests":[{"name":"Uses addEventListener","type":"regex","check":"addEventListener\\(['\"]click['\"]"}]},
        {"id":"m4l3","title":"textContent","type":"lesson","fileName":"text.js","xp":40,"docs":"<p>Set <code>h1</code> text to <code>\"Shipped\"</code></p>","starterCode":"// Set h1 text\n","solution":"const setTitle = () => {\n document.querySelector('h1').textContent = 'Shipped';\n};","hints":[".textContent = 'Shipped'"],"tests":[{"name":"Sets textContent","type":"regex","check":"textContent\\s*=\\s*['\"]Shipped['\"]"}]},
        {"id":"m4l4","title":"Counter Project","type":"project","fileName":"counter.js","xp":60,"docs":"<p><code>let count = 0</code>. Function <code>increment</code> adds 1 and logs</p>","starterCode":"let count = 0;\n// increment function\n","solution":"let count = 0;\nconst increment = () => {\n count++;\n console.log(count);\n};\nincrement();","hints":["count++"],"tests":[{"name":"Declares count","type":"regex","check":"let\\s+count\\s*=\\s*0"},{"name":"Increments count","type":"regex","check":"count\\+\\+"}]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m5",
      "title": "Async & APIs",
      "description": "Fetch data. Promises. async/await.",
      "lessons": [
        {"id":"m5l1","title":"Promises","type":"lesson","fileName":"promise.js","xp":50,"docs":"<p>Create promise that resolves with <code>\"done\"</code>. Log with <code>.then()</code></p>","starterCode":"// Promise\n","solution":"const p = new Promise((resolve) => resolve('done'));\np.then(result => console.log(result));","hints":["new Promise((resolve) =>...)"],"tests":[{"name":"Uses.then","type":"regex","check":"\\.then\\("}]},
        {"id":"m5l2","title":"async/await","type":"lesson","fileName":"async.js","xp":50,"docs":"<p><code>async function getData()</code> awaits <code>Promise.resolve(\"data\")</code></p>","starterCode":"// async function\n","solution":"async function getData() {\n const data = await Promise.resolve('data');\n console.log(data);\n}\ngetData();","hints":["async function","await Promise"],"tests":[{"name":"Uses async","type":"regex","check":"async\\s+function"},{"name":"Uses await","type":"regex","check":"await"}]},
        {"id":"m5l3","title":"Fetch API","type":"lesson","fileName":"fetch.js","xp":60,"docs":"<p>Fetch <code>'https://api.github.com'</code> and log <code>response.status</code></p>","starterCode":"// Fetch API\n","solution":"async function checkAPI() {\n const res = await fetch('https://api.github.com');\n console.log(res.status);\n}\ncheckAPI();","hints":["await fetch()"],"tests":[{"name":"Calls fetch","type":"regex","check":"fetch\\(['\"]https://api\\.github\\.com['\"]\\)"}]},
        {"id":"m5l4","title":"JSON","type":"lesson","fileName":"json.js","xp":50,"docs":"<p>Stringify <code>{ship: true}</code> and log it</p>","starterCode":"// Stringify\n","solution":"const obj = {ship: true};\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(obj));","hints":["JSON.stringify()"],"tests":[{"name":"Logs JSON","type":"log","check":"{\"ship\":true}"}]},
        {"id":"m5l5","title":"API Fetch Project","type":"project","fileName":"api.js","xp":70,"docs":"<p>Fetch <code>'https://api.github.com/zen'</code>, get text, log it</p>","starterCode":"// Fetch Zen\n","solution":"async function getZen() {\n const res = await fetch('https://api.github.com/zen');\n const text = await res.text();\n console.log(text);\n}\ngetZen();","hints":["await res.text()"],"tests":[{"name":"Fetches zen","type":"regex","check":"fetch\\(['\"]https://api\\.github\\.com/zen['\"]\\)"},{"name":"Uses text()","type":"regex","check":"\\.text\\(\\)"}]}
      ]
    }
  ],
